{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0.005,"avg_sec":206.52,"success_pct":0.96},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [[NORMAL]] HARDEN restart coalescer: apply a deferred restart only at a TURN BOUNDARY, never mid-DONE-finalization (close-interruption root, live 2026-06-10). EVIDENCE: 5+ closes today were interrupted by the deferred-restart hard cap - log shows \"otlozhennyj perezapusk primenen po tajmautu: busy-hold prevysil maksimum\" landing mid-close (e.g. 17:58 right after a gate-regression verdict), then the resumed session re-verifies from scratch; done-count stalls while commits keep landing. The coalescer (restart.deferred logic, driver/80-loop-preflight.ps1 and/or Wait-AgentProcess midturn check) correctly DEFERS while busy but its hard cap (~600s) fires regardless of phase. FIX (small, existing mechanism tuning - no new subsystem): (1) when the cap expires, do NOT apply immediately if the driver is inside DONE-finalization (planner verdict received / completion blocks running, e.g. status_text or a state flag set at completion start); instead apply at the NEXT loop-top (turn boundary). (2) raise the hard cap for the apply-at-boundary case to 1800s as a runaway backstop. ACCEPTANCE: a deferred restart with an in-flight DONE-finalization applies only after the close completes or fails (test with a stubbed completion flag); a truly idle driver still applies within the old cap; SelfTest + smoke PASS.","commit":"53ba815ff475a011d54ee0c3df506e7949fad8e2","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-06-10T19:52:58.1372660Z"}
{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0.0002,"avg_sec":32.67,"success_pct":0.0138},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [[NORMAL]] Harden the project-autopilot control-plane gate hole (security/governance, Foundation #2 harden).\n\nROOT INCIDENT: the bridge\u0027s OWN project-autopilot generator built and committed an \"energy-saving idle mode\" that edited control-plane driver.ps1 + driver/81-loop-idle-claim.ps1 with NO operator admission, because project-autopilot items are exempt from the control-plane claim-gate (commit 47e0317). The SAME hole let the \"Checkpoint/Restore\" subsystem edit driver/81-86 + lib/backlog-core.ps1. Both were operator-reverted/rejected. The exemption was meant for the planner/coordinator, NOT for executor atoms touching critical infra.\n\nFIX (atom-sized, one focused change + a regression test): in Test-BacklogApprovedItemClaimable (lib/backlog-core.ps1), the project-autopilot exemption must apply ONLY to the coordinator/planner item, NOT to executor atoms (tag \"atom\") whose files / touch_set hit control-plane paths (driver*.ps1, driver/*.ps1, server.ps1, supervisor.ps1, watchdog.ps1, lib/backlog*.ps1, lib/parallel.ps1, lib/circuit-breaker.ps1). Such atoms must require bridge_self_admission like any other control-plane change. Reconcile the two inconsistent detections (broad Test-IdeaTouchesControlPlane vs narrow Test-ProjectAutopilotControlPlanePath) so one consistent definition is used.\n\nACCEPTANCE: (1) a project-autopilot atom with files=[\"driver.ps1\"] and no admission is NOT claimable (reason control-plane-blocked); (2) the same atom WITH a valid bridge_self_admission IS claimable; (3) a project-autopilot atom touching only non-control-plane files stays claimable; (4) the coordinator/planner item is unaffected. Add tools/test-autopilot-controlplane-gate.ps1 covering all four.","after_turns":192,"after":{"timeout_pct":0.0052,"avg_sec":215.15,"success_pct":0.9688},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-09T00:12:18.0965760Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"worse","ts":"2026-06-10T23:00:03.5545293Z","commit":"8d08e16ef7367276008f4b102fa50978efa739e4"}
